BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet &amp\; Greet with Denise La Neve
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261213T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261213T160000
UID:15f7c00fa0a8897cbe29c73d7bcaffd4@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:Come meet Denise La Neve as she presents the new poetry collec
 tion\, Here There Be Lions (published by The Poet's Press).&nbsp\;This col
 lection is dedicated to the memory and the important lifetime contribution
 s of Jane Goodall. Animals have always companioned us in myth\, fable\, le
 gend and poetry. Here There Be Lions was originally a Latin inscription Hi
 c sunt leoni used to fill blank spaces in world maps\, suggesting that wha
 tever else we did or did not know about terra incognita\, its proper landl
 ords were the beasts. The three editors of this collection ─ Denise La N
 eve\, Paul Nash and Brett Rutherford ─ have selected poems about or insp
 ired by animals. Poets herein range from the ancient Greek poet Archias to
  Geoffrey Chaucer and Walt Whitman\, then on to well-regarded modern and c
 ontemporary poets. Denise La Neve and Paul Nash\, editors of three previou
 s anthologies (The Poets of the Palisades series) invited submissions from
  poets who have been active in the North Jersey poetry series they current
 ly run in Wayne\, NJ. Poets included within these pages: Joel Allegretti\,
  Archias\, Norma Ketzis Bernstock\, Theresa Burns\, Geoffrey Chaucer\, Joh
 n Chorazy\, Catherine Doty\, Jane Ebihara\, RG Evans\, Laura Freedgood\, D
 eborah Gerish\, Suzanne Gili Post\, Boruk Glasgow\, Emilie Glen\, George G
 uida\, Barbara Hall\, Therése Halscheid\, Patrick Hammer\, George C. Harv
 illa\, Pamela Hughe\, Josh Humphrey\, Elizabeth Isacke\, Paul Juszcyk\, Va
 siliki Katsarou\, Tina Kelley\, Elaine Koplow\, Denise La Neve\, Susanna L
 ee\, Timothy Liu\, Diane Lockward\, Roy Lucianna\, Mary Makofske\, Gene My
 ers\, Paul Nash\, Tom Plante\, Shirley Powell\, Morton D. Rich\, Susanna R
 ich\, Eddwin Romond\, Brett Rutherford\, Diane Sahms\, Carole Stone\, John
  J. Trause\, Doris Umbers\, BJ Ward\, Galen Warden\, Walt Whitman\, Joe We
 il\, George Witte\, Anton Yakovlev\, Michael T. Young\, Donald Zirilli smf
  Sander Zulauf. THEME: Author Meet &amp\; Greet HOST: Wayne Public Library
  FEATURES: Denise La Neve PRICE: FREE CONTACT: FB - Wayne Public Library /
  wpladults@waynepubliclibrary.org / (973) 694-4272
LOCATION:Wayne Public Library (Marion Grober StoryTime Room)\, 461 Valley 
 Road\, Wayne\, NJ\, 07470
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/meet-greet-with-denise-la-neve
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
