SUMMARY:First Congregational Church: First OPEN MIC NIGHT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261217T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261217T210000
UID:ebd53ff53c21ccd7048c95f0987d0844@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:Third Thursdays @First is your new home for the vibrant art co
 mmunity—a welcoming space where music\, visual art\, poetry\, and storyt
 elling come alive. First Congregational Church of Westfield invites musici
 ans\, artists\, poets\, and storytellers to join our new open mic series\,
  Third (3rd) Thursdays @ First. Inspired by the creative spirit of the cof
 fee and teahouses of the '90s\, this series is designed for artists and ar
 t lovers to connect\, share\, and celebrate creativity in all its forms. I
 f you are 16 or older\, come as you are and showcase your talent—whether
  through performance\, spoken word\, or visual art. Performers must sign u
 p in advance for a 10-minute slot (first come\, first served). We request 
 a $5 donation from attendees\; coffee\, tea\, and light snacks will be ser
 ved. All proceeds support future open mic nights and community outreach in
 itiatives\, helping to nurture and grow our local art scene. Visit fccofwe
 stfield.org/events to sign up! THEME: OPEN MIC / FEATURES HOST: First Cong
 regational Church of Westfield\, NJ FEATURES: Performers must sign up in a
 dvance for a 10-minute slot (first come\, first served). PRICE: $5 Donatio
 n from attendees\; coffee\, tea\, and light snacks will be served. CONTACT
 : Visit fccofwestfield.org/events to sign up! / FB - First Congregational 
 Church of Westfield\, NJ
LOCATION:First Congregational Church\, 125 Elmer Street\, Westfield\, NJ\,
  07090
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/third-thursdays-first-open-mic
 -night-dec
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Story &amp\; Verse: A Storytelling and Poetic Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261217T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261217T210000
UID:3e2e850ea9661a2cbeb5c59fe7a05aee@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:Name of Event: &nbsp\;Story &amp\; Verse: A Storytelling and P
 oetic Open Mic Date: &nbsp\;December 17\, 2026 Start/End Time: &nbsp\;7:00
  pm - 9:00 pm Address: &nbsp\;102 Witherspoon Street\, Princeton\, NJ 0854
 2 Theme: &nbsp\;Reverly Host: &nbsp\;Brass Rabbit Price: &nbsp\;FREE Phone
 : &nbsp\; (609) 924-8777 Email Address: &nbsp\; fclark@artscouncilofprince
 ton.org Website: &nbsp\; http://artscouncilofprinceton.org/event/story-ver
 se-a-storytelling-and-poetic-open-mic-oct26/ Social Media: &nbsp\; @artsco
 uncilofprinceton Event Description: &nbsp\;Share your story\, your poetry\
 , or your prose\, based on the monthly theme! Story &amp\; Verse provides 
 a warm and welcoming spotlight for both emerging and established artists i
 n our Solley Theater\, an intimate space in the heart of Downtown Princeto
 n. Join us as a performer: Prepare a story\, poem\, or spoken word piece u
 p to 5 minutes in length and (at least loosely) related to the theme. This
  month’s theme is “Reverly“ Arrive by 6:45pm to add your name to the
  hat. No previous experience or pre-registration necessary. Join our audie
 nce: Take the elevator or stairs to the Solley Theater\, located on the to
 p floor of our Paul Robeson Center for the Arts. Optional: participate fro
 m your seat with a Micro Story. Read the printed prompt based on the eveni
 ng’s theme and respond with a super concise story (just a line or two!) 
 that answers the question. Brass Rabbit will read your story at the mic\, 
 as time allows. Find a seat and enjoy the performances. We kick off shortl
 y after 7pm.
LOCATION:102 Witherspoon Lane\, Princeton\, NJ\, 08542
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/story-verse-a-storytelling-and
 -poetic-open-mic-dec
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
